    "result_text": "There's a single test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` derived field on owners, mapping the locality/region to an IANA timezone name via the fixed table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `timezone` property (read-only string) to the Owner schema, right after `locality`, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`CityRegionResolver.java`** \u2014 Added the fixed `REGION_TIMEZONE` table and a `timezoneForRegion(String region)` method returning the IANA name, or `null` for a region not in the table. This keeps the region-keyed lookups colocated with the existing city/postcode tables, consistent with the class's single-source-of-truth design.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", ...)` and a `timezone(Owner)` method that derives the value from the owner's existing `locality(owner)` region, so `timezone` always agrees with the reported `locality`.\n\nThe suite (`AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion`, which asserts `locality=NSW` and `timezone=Australia/Sydney` for a Sydney owner) is green: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**.",
